{"agent_id":"pp3g-CCZy-review-r2-luna-durability-154-durable-fork-d2a2","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:31:34.853531319Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c1dd8493-501b-4913-8257-e4da32d05913","comment_uuid":"8c1e195f-21bf-42ef-b97b-7216e33eb10e","author":"pp3g-CCZy-review-r2-luna-durability-154-durable-fork-d2a2","content":"## Review Summary: FAIL\n\n### MUST FIX (blocking)\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:350 and /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/processor.ts:660-674 — the claimed 3-POST invariant is not global. The outer schedule caps its own errors in /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts:30-55,208-242, but streamText still accepts maxRetries=input.retries??0; callers pass retries:2 at /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts:225-235 and /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/handlers/project-copy.ts:34-51. WHY: per-layer counters do not establish a wire-attempt bound. WHAT: fixed-harness server log records POST#1..#4 while client terminal reports attempt=3/totalPOSTs=3: /tmp/opencode-matrix.QB3Ubr/server-row1.log:2-9 and client-row1.out:40-47; matrix summary: /tmp/opencode/matrix-run/matrix-fixed-harness-235.log:72-89. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based that four POSTs occurred; not proven whether POST#4 is SDK retry or an in-flight cleanup request. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: no request/attempt correlation or clean run with SDK retries independently disabled. Fix: one global budget, normally maxRetries:0 for this path, request IDs/attempt IDs, and a clean wire-count proof.\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/cli/upgrade.ts:8-42 and /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/installation/index.ts:265-313 — upgrade survival is procedural, not enforced. autoupdate:false is only a config short-circuit and install upgrades replace the direct binary. The operational artifact specifies manual drift checking, not an executable wrapper/REAL indirection: /tmp/opencode/opencode-fork-draft.md:73-78,107-118. WHY: upgrade/config loss can silently remove the fix. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: live PATH and simulated upgrade. Fix: stable wrapper, marker check before exec, fail-closed drift handling.\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/install:327-352 — installer is neither rollback-safe nor atomic: direct mv/cp over target, no backup or staged same-filesystem rename. The backup/mv procedure is prose only: /tmp/opencode/opencode-fork-draft.md:90-105. Fix: verify staged file, retain versioned backup, atomic rename, verify marker/hash, preserve old target on failure.\n\n### SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:43-59 — safeIterable removes the observed finalizer deadlock, but fire-and-forget return can leave a hanging/rejecting iterator and transport alive beyond the Effect scope; throw() is not forwarded. WHY: abort/interrupt/compaction/concurrency require bounded cleanup. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based risk, not demonstrated leak. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: no stress run with hanging return plus concurrent requests. Add bounded observable cleanup/cancellation.\n\n### NITS\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts:213-224 — totalPOSTs is an outer attempt index, not a measured wire count; rename unless correlated.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:36-60,414-415 targets the reproduced Effect finalizer deadlock; gate evidence shows visible Body read timed out/ERROR rather than exit 124.\n- /tmp/opencode/fork-build/packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts:62-92,213-242 preserves retry-after and scopes the budget to named codes.\n- /tmp/opencode/matrix-run/run-matrix.sh:152-173,197-216 has useful slow-progress, stalled, and parsed-stream coverage.\n\nOverall: FAIL for the requested durability gate; stream-deadlock fix is conditionally supported, but global wire bound, wrapper indirection, and atomic rollback remain unproven/unimplemented.","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:31:34.843449749Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:IXxpOt8RBzI9JT23rKj5zNaG112UysN06RUprMq/9V8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNCEP4fOo+8SQVqRfyfWWUEmA/PLUD+MfVuFjhbzET00AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAWK9QXq9fCnzup3KzPhm0RVxCQyt4ZRkUQntDNjV4JnJc6qS7BsGfu5Wwdgo1otW56iPFB/2UaplE1oREehsbBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:IXxpOt8RBzI9JT23rKj5zNaG112UysN06RUprMq/9V8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNCEP4fOo+8SQVqRfyfWWUEmA/PLUD+MfVuFjhbzET00AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIYLPa6ZaA4HiPWobkwngH13Y7AHfKqv5g/xsWYuEOFs0/Cixmdtb/+mQjLfR2jaLTik62MhagxOtRTKt+vTlgY="}
